IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha-types`
IMPORT `ha-pay`
IMPORT `ha-annual`

-- Holidays Act 2003 — GOAL 3: PUBLIC HOLIDAYS AND ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAYS.
--
--   "Which days are the employee's public holidays; what must the employer
--    pay for one, worked or not; does the employee earn an alternative
--    holiday; and what is paid for that?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_129.txt — ss 44-61A,
-- 12(4), 40(3).

§ `Goal 3 — public holidays`

§§ `The days (s 44)`

-- s 44(1)(f), (g) "Good Friday: Easter Monday:". The Act does not say how
-- Easter is found; the encoding uses the Gregorian computus (the anonymous
-- algorithm of Meeus, Jones and Butcher), which gives the Western Easter
-- Sunday on which New Zealand observes them.
@ref s 44(1)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` y MEANS
    Date (((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) MODULO 31) PLUS 1) (FLOOR ((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) DIVIDED BY 31)) y
    WHERE
        a MEANS y MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS y MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        m MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)

GIVEN month IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first Monday of month` month `in` y MEANS
    Date (1 PLUS ((8 MINUS `Weekday of` (Date 1 month y)) MODULO 7)) month y

-- s 44(1) "The following days are public holidays: (a) Christmas Day: (b)
-- Boxing Day: (c) New Year's Day: (d) 2 January: Waitangi Day: Good Friday:
-- Easter Monday: ANZAC Day: the birthday of the reigning Sovereign (observed
-- on the first Monday in June): the day on which a public holiday is
-- observed to acknowledge Matariki ...: Labour Day (being the fourth Monday
-- in October): the day of the anniversary of a province or the day locally
-- observed as that day."
@ref s 44(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday`, cal IS A `Calendar inputs`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` p `falls on, calendar` cal MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `(a) Christmas Day`                 THEN Date 25 12 y
    WHEN `(b) Boxing Day`                    THEN Date 26 12 y
    WHEN `(c) New Year's Day`                THEN Date 1 1 y
    WHEN `(d) 2 January`                     THEN Date 2 1 y
    WHEN `Waitangi Day`                      THEN Date 6 2 y
    WHEN `Good Friday`                       THEN `the day` (0 MINUS 2) `days after` (`Easter Sunday in` y)
    WHEN `Easter Monday`                     THEN `the day` 1 `days after` (`Easter Sunday in` y)
    WHEN `ANZAC Day`                         THEN Date 25 4 y
    WHEN `the Sovereign's birthday`          THEN `the first Monday of month` 6 `in` y
    WHEN `Matariki Observance Day`           THEN cal's `Matariki Observance Day that year`
    WHEN `Labour Day`                        THEN `the day` 21 `days after` (`the first Monday of month` 10 `in` y)
    WHEN `the anniversary of a province`     THEN cal's `anniversary day observed locally that year`
    WHERE
        y MEANS cal's `calendar year`

`every public holiday` MEANS
    LIST `(a) Christmas Day`, `(b) Boxing Day`, `(c) New Year's Day`, `(d) 2 January`,
         `Waitangi Day`, `Good Friday`, `Easter Monday`, `ANZAC Day`,
         `the Sovereign's birthday`, `Matariki Observance Day`, `Labour Day`,
         `the anniversary of a province`

§§ `Mondayisation (ss 45, 45A)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, cal IS A `Calendar inputs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `would otherwise be a working day, by the usual weekdays` d cal IF
    elem (`Weekday of` d) (cal's `weekdays the employee would otherwise work`)

-- s 45(1) "if any of the public holidays listed in section 44(1)(a) to
-- (d)— (a) falls on a Saturday and the day would otherwise be a working day
-- for the employee, the public holiday must be treated as falling on that
-- day: (b) falls on a Saturday and the day would not otherwise be a working
-- day ..., the public holiday must be treated as falling on the following
-- Monday: (c) falls on a Sunday and the day would otherwise be a working day
-- ..., ... on that day: (d) falls on a Sunday and the day would not
-- otherwise be a working day ..., ... on the following Tuesday."
-- s 45A(1) "if Waitangi Day or ANZAC Day— (a) falls on a Saturday or a
-- Sunday, and the day would otherwise be a working day ..., ... on that day:
-- (b) falls on a Saturday or a Sunday, and the day would not otherwise be a
-- working day ..., ... on the following Monday."
@ref ss 45, 45A
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday`, cal IS A `Calendar inputs`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` p `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `would otherwise be a working day, by the usual weekdays` actual cal THEN actual
        IF christmasToJanuary AND w EQUALS Saturday THEN `the day` 2 `days after` actual
        IF christmasToJanuary AND w EQUALS Sunday   THEN `the day` 2 `days after` actual
        IF waitangiOrAnzac    AND w EQUALS Saturday THEN `the day` 2 `days after` actual
        IF waitangiOrAnzac    AND w EQUALS Sunday   THEN `the day` 1 `days after` actual
        OTHERWISE actual
    WHERE
        actual MEANS `the day` p `falls on, calendar` cal
        w      MEANS `Weekday of` actual
        christmasToJanuary MEANS
               p EQUALS `(a) Christmas Day` OR p EQUALS `(b) Boxing Day`
            OR p EQUALS `(c) New Year's Day` OR p EQUALS `(d) 2 January`
        waitangiOrAnzac MEANS p EQUALS `Waitangi Day` OR p EQUALS `ANZAC Day`

-- s 44(2) "If 2 or more of the public holidays specified in subsection (1)
-- fall on the same day, the public holidays must, for the purposes of this
-- subpart, be treated as 1 day." FORK F10: this applies to the days the
-- holidays are treated as falling on after ss 45 and 45A, so ANZAC Day on a
-- Sunday, moved to an Easter Monday, gives one public holiday.
-- s 44(1)(ia), Matariki, has been a public holiday since 2022; the list as it
-- stood before is not carried.
@ref ss 44, 45, 45A
@export The employee's public holidays in a calendar year under ss 44, 45 and 45A of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ), from 2022: the twelve days of s 44(1), with Christmas, Boxing Day, New Year's Day and 2 January moved to the following Monday (or Tuesday) and Waitangi Day and ANZAC Day to the following Monday when they fall on a weekend day the employee would not otherwise work, and holidays on the same day counted once. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN cal IS A `Calendar inputs`  @desc The year, the date of Matariki Observance Day that year (Te Kāhui o Matariki Public Holiday Act 2022, Schedule 1), the local anniversary day, and the weekdays the employee would otherwise work (0 Sunday to 6 Saturday)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the public holidays for the employee in` cal MEANS
    IF   cal's `calendar year` AT LEAST 2022
    THEN nub (map (GIVEN p YIELD `the day` p `is treated as falling on, calendar` cal) `every public holiday`)
    ELSE `before 2022 the list of public holidays was not the one this version of s 44(1) gives`

`before 2022 the list of public holidays was not the one this version of s 44(1) gives` MEANS
    REFUSE "before 2022 the list of public holidays was not the one this version of s 44(1) gives"

GIVEN d IS A DATE, cal IS A `Calendar inputs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a public holiday for the employee` d cal IF
    elem d (`the public holidays for the employee in` cal)

§§ `Transfers (ss 44A-44C)`

-- s 44B(1) "An employer and employee may agree in writing ... that a public
-- holiday ... is to be observed by the employee on another calendar day or
-- during a period of 24 hours ..., if the criteria in subsection (2) are
-- met". (2) "(a) the public holiday ... (i) is identified; and (ii) would
-- otherwise be a working day ...; and (b) the calendar day or period of 24
-- hours ... (i) is identified or identifiable; and (ii) would otherwise be a
-- working day ...; and (iii) is not another public holiday or part of a
-- public holiday; and (c) the purpose of the transfer is not to avoid the
-- employee's entitlements under sections 50 and 56". s 44C(3) "If an
-- employer adopts a policy ..., sections 44A and 44B do not apply".
@ref ss 44B, 44C
GIVEN t IS A `Whole transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the whole transfer is valid` t IF
        NOT t's `a policy under s 44C covers that part of the business for the whole transfer`
    AND t's `agreed in writing`
    AND t's `the public holiday is identified`
    AND t's `the public holiday would otherwise be a working day`
    AND t's `the new day is identified or identifiable`
    AND t's `the new day would otherwise be a working day`
    AND NOT t's `the new day is another public holiday or part of one`
    AND NOT t's `the purpose is to avoid the entitlements under ss 50 and 56`

-- s 44A(1) "This section applies if— (a) an employee is to start work on a
-- day and finish work on the following day; and (b) one or both of those
-- days are specified in section 44(1)." (2) "may agree in writing", (2)(b)
-- each 24-hour period "is to start or finish during the day ... and includes
-- the period from when the employee is to start work to when the employee is
-- to finish work". (3) "the purpose of the transfer is not to avoid".
@ref ss 44A, 44C
GIVEN t IS A `Part transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the part transfer is valid` t IF
        NOT t's `a policy under s 44C covers that part of the business for the part transfer`
    AND t's `the employee starts work on one day and finishes on the next`
    AND t's `one or both days are public holidays`
    AND t's `part transfer agreed in writing`
    AND t's `each 24-hour period starts or finishes on the public holiday and covers the shift`
    AND NOT t's `the purpose of the part transfer is to avoid the entitlements under ss 50 and 56`

§§ `Working, and pay (ss 47-55, 59, 61A)`

-- s 47 "An employer may require an employee to work on a public holiday if—
-- (a) the public holiday falls on a day on which, but for it being a public
-- holiday, would otherwise be a working day for the employee; and (b) the
-- employee is required to work on the public holiday under the employee's
-- employment agreement."
@ref s 47
GIVEN `otherwise working` IS A BOOLEAN, `required by the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may require work on the public holiday, otherwise a working day:` `otherwise working` `, required by the agreement:` `required by the agreement` IF
    `otherwise working` AND `required by the agreement`

-- s 61A(1) "This section applies to an employee who is required, or has
-- agreed, to work on a public holiday but who does not work on the day
-- because— (a) the employee— (i) becomes or remains sick or injured; or (ii)
-- has a spouse or partner or dependant who becomes or remains sick or
-- injured; or (b) ... suffers ... a bereavement ...; or (c) ... becomes
-- entitled to take family violence leave".
@ref s 61A(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday worked or not`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61A applies to` p IF
        p's `the employee was required or had agreed to work`
    AND NOT p's `the employee worked any part of the day under the agreement`
    AND NOT p's `reason the employee did not work` EQUALS `any other reason`

-- s 50(1) "the employer must pay the employee the greater of— (a) the
-- portion of the employee's relevant daily pay or average daily pay (less
-- any penal rates) that relates to the time actually worked on the day plus
-- half that amount again; or (b) the portion of the employee's relevant
-- daily pay that relates to the time actually worked on the day."
@ref s 50
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday worked or not`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay for working on the public holiday under s 50` p MEANS
    max ((p's `portion of the daily pay for the time actually worked` MINUS p's `penal rates within that portion`) TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 2)
        (p's `portion of relevant daily pay for the time actually worked`)

-- s 49 "If an employee does not work on a public holiday and the day would
-- otherwise be a working day for the employee, the employer must pay the
-- employee not less than the employee's relevant daily pay or average daily
-- pay for that day." s 61A(2)(b)(i) "must be paid for the day in accordance
-- with section 49 and is not entitled to be paid at time and a half". s
-- 48(1) a day not otherwise a working day, not worked: nothing is payable.
@ref ss 48, 49, 50, 61A
@export The least the employer must pay for a public holiday under ss 48-50 and 61A of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ): if the employee works any part of it, the greater of time and a half on the daily pay for the time worked (less penal rates) and relevant daily pay for that time (s 50); if not, and it would otherwise be a working day, the relevant or average daily pay (s 49), including when the employee was to work but was sick, bereaved or on family violence leave (s 61A); otherwise nothing. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday worked or not`  @desc The day as it fell for the employee: whether it would otherwise be a working day, whether they worked any part of it, whether they were required or had agreed to work and why they did not, on-call status, the daily pay facts, and the pay for the time worked (at daily pay, its penal rates, and at relevant daily pay)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay for the public holiday` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `the employee worked any part of the day under the agreement`
            THEN `the pay for working on the public holiday under s 50` p
        IF p's `would otherwise be a working day for the employee`
            THEN `the daily pay` (p's `daily pay for the public holiday`)
        OTHERWISE 0

-- s 56(1) "An employee is entitled to another day's holiday (an alternative
-- holiday) instead of a public holiday if— (a) the public holiday falls on a
-- day that would otherwise be a working day for an employee; and (b) the
-- employee works ... on any part of that day." (4) "An employee is not
-- entitled to an alternative holiday under this section if the employee
-- works for the employer only on public holidays." s 59(2) on call and
-- called in; (3) on call, not called in, but "for all practical purposes,
-- the employee has not had a whole holiday". s 61A(2)(b)(ii) "is not
-- entitled to an alternative holiday".
@ref ss 56, 59, 61A
@export Whether the employee earns an alternative holiday for a public holiday under ss 56, 59 and 61A of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ): only if the day would otherwise be a working day and the employee worked any part of it, or was on call and either called in or so restricted that they had no whole holiday; never for an employee who works, or is on call, only on public holidays. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday worked or not`  @desc The day as it fell for the employee: whether it would otherwise be a working day, whether they worked any part of it, whether they work only on public holidays, and their on-call status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee earns an alternative holiday for` p IF
        p's `would otherwise be a working day for the employee`
    AND NOT p's `works for the employer only on public holidays`
    AND (    p's `the employee worked any part of the day under the agreement`
         OR  p's `on call status` EQUALS `(2) on call and called in to work`
         OR  p's `on call status` EQUALS `(3) on call, not called in, and for all practical purposes not a whole holiday`)

-- s 48 "(1) If a public holiday falls on a day that would not otherwise be a
-- working day ..., section 46 is complied with if— (a) the employee does not
-- work on the day; or (b) the employee works on any part of the day and the
-- employer pays the employee in accordance with section 50. (2) If a public
-- holiday falls on a day that would otherwise be a working day ..., section
-- 46 is complied with if— (a) the employee— (i) does not work on that day;
-- and (ii) the employer pays the employee in accordance with section 49; or
-- (b) the employee— (i) works ... on any part of that day; and (ii) the
-- employer pays the employee in accordance with section 50; and (iii) the
-- employer provides the employee with an alternative holiday under section
-- 56."
@ref ss 46, 48
GIVEN p IS A `Public holiday worked or not`, paid IS A NUMBER, `alternative given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46 is complied with for` p `, paid` paid `, alternative holiday provided:` `alternative given` IF
        paid AT LEAST `the pay for the public holiday` p
    AND ((NOT `the employee earns an alternative holiday for` p) OR `alternative given`)

-- s 55 "An employer must pay an employee for a public holiday in the pay that
-- relates to the pay period in which the holiday occurs."
@ref s 55
`when public holiday pay is due` MEANS `in the pay for the pay period in which the holiday or leave falls`

§§ `Agreements and the s 50 provision (ss 51-53)`

-- s 52 "(1) This section applies to an employment agreement that is entered
-- into after 1 April 2004. (2) The employment agreement must include a
-- provision that confirms the right of the employee to be paid in accordance
-- with section 50". s 53(3) the date for an existing agreement: "(a) for an
-- existing collective agreement to which section 51 applies, the later of—
-- (i) 1 April 2007; or (ii) the date on which a collective agreement that
-- replaces the existing collective agreement comes into force: (b) for an
-- existing individual employment agreement to which section 51 applies, 1
-- April 2007: (c) for all other existing employment agreements, the earlier
-- of— (i) the date on which the existing employment agreement is next
-- amended; or (ii) 1 April 2005."
-- An agreement entered into on 1 April 2004 is neither "before" (s 5) nor
-- "after" (s 52(1)) that day; the encoding refuses it.
@ref ss 52, 53
GIVEN entered IS A DATE, `collective with s 51` IS A BOOLEAN, `individual with s 51` IS A BOOLEAN, replaced IS A MAYBE DATE, amended IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the agreement must confirm the s 50 right, entered` entered `, existing collective with s 51:` `collective with s 51` `, existing individual with s 51:` `individual with s 51` `, replaced` replaced `, next amended` amended MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF entered GREATER THAN Date 1 4 2004 THEN entered
        IF entered EQUALS Date 1 4 2004 THEN `an agreement entered into on 1 April 2004 is neither existing (s 5) nor entered into after that day (s 52(1))`
        IF `collective with s 51` THEN
            CONSIDER replaced
            WHEN JUST r THEN IF r GREATER THAN Date 1 4 2007 THEN r ELSE Date 1 4 2007
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the existing collective agreement has not been replaced, so the s 53(3)(a) date is not yet fixed`
        IF `individual with s 51` THEN Date 1 4 2007
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER amended
            WHEN JUST a THEN IF a LESS THAN Date 1 4 2005 THEN a ELSE Date 1 4 2005
            WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 1 4 2005

`an agreement entered into on 1 April 2004 is neither existing (s 5) nor entered into after that day (s 52(1))` MEANS
    REFUSE "an agreement entered into on 1 April 2004 is neither existing (s 5) nor entered into after that day (s 52(1))"

`the existing collective agreement has not been replaced, so the s 53(3)(a) date is not yet fixed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the existing collective agreement has not been replaced, so the s 53(3)(a) date is not yet fixed"

§§ `Alternative holidays (ss 57, 60, 61)`

-- s 57(1) "An alternative holiday provided under section 56 must— (a) be
-- taken by the employee on a day that is agreed ...; and (b) be a day that
-- would otherwise be a working day ...; and (c) be a whole working day off
-- work ...; and (d) not be taken on a public holiday." (2) If they cannot
-- agree, "the day must be taken on a date determined, on a reasonable basis,
-- by the employer". (3) "at least 14 days' notice". Whether the employer's
-- choice is reasonable is an input (it is the notice that is checked).
@ref s 57
GIVEN a IS AN `Alternative holiday`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the alternative holiday meets s 57` a IF
        (    a's `the day was agreed`
         OR  CONSIDER a's `notice of the day given on`
             WHEN JUST n THEN `not less than 14 days' notice, given` n `, for` (a's `alternative holiday taken on`)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    AND a's `the day would otherwise be a working day`
    AND a's `a whole working day off`
    AND NOT a's `the day is a public holiday`

-- s 60(1) "An employer must pay an employee not less than the employee's
-- relevant daily pay or average daily pay for the day which is taken as the
-- alternative holiday." (2)(a) "in the pay that relates to the pay period in
-- which the alternative holiday is taken".
@ref s 60
GIVEN a IS AN `Alternative holiday`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay for the alternative holiday` a MEANS
    `the daily pay` (a's `daily pay on the alternative holiday`)

-- s 60(2)(b) "if the employee has not taken the alternative holiday before
-- the date on which his or her employment ends,— (i) at the rate of the
-- employee's relevant daily pay or average daily pay for his or her last day
-- of employment; and (ii) in the pay that relates to the employee's final
-- period of employment."
@ref s 60(2)(b)
GIVEN e IS AN `End of employment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay for alternative holidays not taken at the end of` e MEANS
    e's `alternative holidays not taken` TIMES `the daily pay` (e's `daily pay on the last day of employment`)

-- s 61(2) "A request ... (a) may be made only if 12 months have passed since
-- the employee's entitlement to the alternative holiday arose". (3) "If the
-- employer agrees ..., the employer must pay the employee the amount agreed".
-- (4) "as soon as practicable". FORK F6 again: the first anniversary is the
-- first day on which 12 months have passed.
@ref s 61
GIVEN r IS AN `Exchange request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee may request the exchange` r IF
    r's `exchange requested on` AT LEAST `add years` (r's `entitlement to the alternative holiday arose on`) 1

@ref s 61
GIVEN r IS AN `Exchange request`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment in exchange for the alternative holiday` r MEANS
    IF   `the employee may request the exchange` r AND r's `the employer agrees to exchange`
    THEN r's `amount agreed in exchange`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Public holidays in untaken annual holidays (s 40(2)-(3))`

-- s 40(3) "The employee is entitled to be paid for a public holiday if the
-- holiday would have— (a) otherwise been a working day for the employee;
-- and (b) occurred during the employee's annual holidays had the employee
-- taken his or her remaining annual holidays entitlement immediately after
-- the date on which the employee's employment came to an end."
-- Walk forward from the day after the end: a working day that is a public
-- holiday counts (s 40(1): it is not part of the annual holidays); any other
-- working day uses one day of the entitlement.
@ref s 40(1), (3)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, remaining IS A NUMBER, cal IS A `Calendar inputs`, holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`count the public holidays from` d `with` remaining `days left, calendar` cal `, holidays` holidays MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF remaining AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        IF NOT `would otherwise be a working day, by the usual weekdays` d cal
            THEN `count the public holidays from` (`the day` 1 `days after` d) `with` remaining `days left, calendar` cal `, holidays` holidays
        IF elem d holidays
            THEN 1 PLUS `count the public holidays from` (`the day` 1 `days after` d) `with` remaining `days left, calendar` cal `, holidays` holidays
        OTHERWISE `count the public holidays from` (`the day` 1 `days after` d) `with` (remaining MINUS 1) `days left, calendar` cal `, holidays` holidays

-- The public holidays of the year the employment ends and of the next year,
-- since the notional holiday may run past 31 December.
@ref s 40(3)
GIVEN ended IS A DATE, `days untaken` IS A NUMBER, cal IS A `Calendar inputs`, `next year` IS A `Calendar inputs`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the public holidays in the notional holiday after` ended `, working days untaken` `days untaken` `, this year` cal `, next year` `next year` MEANS
    IF   null (cal's `weekdays the employee would otherwise work`)
    THEN `an employee with no working weekdays has no notional holiday to place`
    ELSE `count the public holidays from` (`the day` 1 `days after` ended) `with` `days untaken` `days left, calendar` cal `, holidays` (append (`the public holidays for the employee in` cal) (`the public holidays for the employee in` `next year`))

`an employee with no working weekdays has no notional holiday to place` MEANS
    REFUSE "an employee with no working weekdays has no notional holiday to place"
